{"name":"French Manicure","hex":"#fee6dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"french","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare food by cutting it into strips.","To kiss (another person) while inserting one’s tongue into the other person's mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/french"},{"term":"manicure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cosmetic treatment for the fingernails.","A manicurist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply such a treatment to the hands.","To polish or trim something very finely or evenly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manicure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Manicure","blocks":[{"text":"A manicure is a mostly cosmetic beauty treatment for the fingernails and hands performed at home or in a nail salon. A manicure usually consists of filing and shaping the free edge of nails, pushing and clipping any nonliving tissue at the cuticle and removing hangnails, treatments with various liquids, massage of the hand, and the application of fingernail polish. When the same is applied to the toenails and feet, the treatment is referred to as a pedicure. Together, the treatments may be known as a mani-pedi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Hastings_County_Archives_OSD_1938-1939-54_%2839912414015%29.jpg/330px-Hastings_County_Archives_OSD_1938-1939-54_%2839912414015%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manicure"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Manicure_closeup.jpg/330px-Manicure_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Manicure_closeup.jpg/330px-Manicure_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Manicure closeup –clear nail polish being applied","link":"https:/